.	http://purl.oclc.org/NET/cmcs/schema/:hasConfigurations		<rdf:Bag xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" > <rdf:li><rdf:href xlink:href="Parameters/chemsys.mvm" xlink:type="simple"></rdf:href></rdf:li><rdf:li><rdf:href xlink:href="Parameters/BasisSet.ecce_basisset" xlink:type="simple"></rdf:href></rdf:li><rdf:li><rdf:href xlink:href="Parameters/SetupParams" xlink:type="simple"></rdf:href></rdf:li></rdf:Bag>
.	http://www.emsl.pnl.gov/ecce:annotation		ORCA, PBE0-D3BJ/def2-SVP with CPCM(water), VeryTightOpt optimisation and analytic frequencies with IR and Raman. This calculation shows the S-O stretches of a sulfate bridging two cobalt centres in [(en)2Co(mu-OH)(mu-SO4)Co(en)2]3+: the antisymmetric stretch of the two S-O bonds to cobalt at 980.89 cm-1 (unscaled; IR 873.68 km/mol, Raman activity 12.168), their in-phase stretch at 962.38 cm-1 (IR 270.83 km/mol, Raman activity 15.564), and, mainly, the stretch of the S-O bond of 1.489 Angstrom to the oxygen that is not bound to cobalt at 1077.89 cm-1 (IR 417.97 km/mol, Raman activity 28.735). The S-O bonds to cobalt are 1.540 Angstrom long and the two Co-O(sulfate) distances are 1.908 and 1.909 Angstrom. The lowest frequency is 48.53 cm-1; there are no imaginary frequencies.
.	http://www.emsl.pnl.gov/ecce:application		ORCA
